ese are pdx models from from patients  with aml  that have been transplanted into mice  and the first thing we did with these  models  in under the the plot that says jq1  naive is we measured their baseline  sensitivity  to abt-199 which you can see in maroon  but also to two other drugs  s63 845 and the drug that begins with  a133  which are inhibitors of mcl1 and bcl  excel respectively  what you can hopefully appreciate is  that these drugs have  modest um these cells have modest  sensitivity  to these insults but that if you take  the same cells you put them into a mouse  and treat them with jq1 until they  relapse  now you take the cells back out and what  we find is that they indeed  have exhibit increased sensitivity to  abt-199  so the same priming or sensitization  to abt-199 that we observe in in our  crispr screens  and in our evolved resistant cell lines  in vitro we also  see in a pdx model in vivo and that's  also  seen in the in the gi 50 plot that's  shown on the right  now these results suggest that  combination therapies involving jq1  combined with 199  which might be particularly interesting  in the setting of aml  because the resistance to jq1  necessarily creates a scenario  where aml cells become sensitive to 199  and to  test that in a little bit more detail we  did a study  where we examined the effect of the  sequence with which  aml's are treated with these two drugs  and what effect that has  on tumor burden so we took five  different cohorts of mice and we treated  them with vehicle  abc199 alone jq1 alone abt-199  followed by jq1 which is a treatment  sequence that we would not predict  to select for cells that would be  hypersensitive to the second drug  or jq1 followed by 199 which is a  treatment sequence where we would  predict  that resistance to the first drug would  lead to hypersensitivity to the second  drug  now if you do these these experiments  and then you look in the bone marrow of  the mice  what you find is that indeed the the the  the burden  um of uh  of aml cells in the bone marrow is  markedly lower in the setting of jq1  treatment followed by 199 treatment as  compared to all other treatment groups  as is the abundance of cd13 cd33  uh positive cells in the bone marrow and  this is basically a result that's  consistent with the idea  that this this sequential therapy of jq1  followed by 199  is leading to the apototic cell death  rather than a d  differentiation process in these amls  now this entire story as we were putting  it together was very interesting to us  for another reason and that is that it  hearkened very much to a separate study  that we had  published a couple of years ago in the  second melanoma  so in the upper left of this plot i  remind our of this slide i remind you of  the results that we have in  aml where we find that resistance to jq1  leads to hyperactivation of mick and  quan  and consequent sensitization to bcl2  family inhibitors  now in the upper right of this slide  what you see is a different finding  published in 2017 where we observed that  melanoma cells with activating b  ref mutations when treated chronically  with  um inhibitors of braf or braf mech  signaling  develop resistance that is on always in  our hands associated  with the hyper activation of mick as  read out by increased mick protein  levels and so what you can see here  for each cell line uh for example  starting with colo 679  we have mic levels in the parental cells  parental cells upon short-term treatment  with a raf inhibitor where mick is down  regulated  mick is after all a uh a target of the  map kinase pathway  um and then resistant cells that remain  under drug  selection pressure where in this setting  we always find  not only activation reactivation of mick  but really hyperactivation of mic  relative to parental cells  now what these two studies both  suggested to us um through through  separate and extensive studies that i'm  i'm going to gloss over here  is that